One erva-doce tea source, distinct from `@foeniculum-vulgare`. Direct-sow identified culinary seed shallowly in a mild-to-warm growing window, thinning to roughly 15–25 cm. Provide drainage, early weed control, and moisture while establishing. Allow flowers to set the aromatic seed-like fruits. Harvest umbels as fruits turn brown, often after several months from sowing, before shedding; dry with airflow, thresh, and store dry. Keep a labelled viable seed lot for renewal. Do not substitute unidentified ornamental Apiaceae or infer identity from a tea's aroma alone.
} r_0SMBMR83S66S9TPMFWJA9X9FPJ

