Vinagreira supplies leaves for cuxá; other cultivars supply fleshy calyces. Sow about 1–2 cm deep in warm conditions and allow roughly 0.6–1 m for mature plants. Weed early and maintain water through establishment and harvest. Cut young leafy shoots after establishment while leaving nodes for regrowth. Calyx harvest follows flowering and depends strongly on cultivar and day length; collect fleshy sound calyces before they dry around the seed capsule. Dry or process hygienically. Save fully mature seed separately and renew the annual crop, containing volunteers.
} r_7W6HDCMXA3EBPH51VTQT3WWRXF

Turmeric — Curcuma longa (@curcuma-longa: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-dish-crops, #source @farm-source-panc) { r_4M9ZX6Z51DF29JTMRXPSX0FBSN
Açafrão-da-terra is distinct from Crocus saffron. Plant healthy budded rhizome pieces about 5–8 cm deep at reliable warm-season moisture, roughly 25–40 cm apart with row access. Mulch, weed early, and maintain moisture without waterlogging. Lift rhizomes when shoots yellow and die back, commonly 8–10 months after planting; trial-dig rather than relying on a calendar alone. Clean and use fresh or follow an established curing, drying, and milling process for spice. Keep healthy sound rhizomes for the next planting and reject rotted material.
} r_4M9ZX6Z51DF29JTMRXPSX0FBSN

