An identified leafy ingredient of some tacacá preparations. Sow tiny seed shallowly in warmth or root healthy shoots; plant about 20–30 cm apart in moist draining soil. Keep seedlings watered and weeded, then cut tender shoots after establishment, often around 40–60 days after sowing, leaving nodes for regrowth. Flower heads and leaves have distinct culinary uses. Wash and prepare through the established dish process, using correctly identified food stock. Reserve healthy mature flower heads for seed or maintain clean rooted replacements, then clear declining plants.
} r_1Q3RJ0XQGJDNXF8ND5CAD5AMSD
